From 5c1b84b1d5310252e82d068cddaf2c12051dfbef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:01:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 232/274] V2 runner: sample, verify and detect sinks with the
 TileLang kernels

The Gumbel sampler and temperature, the sink detector's candidates and
policy, DSpark's greedy reductions and greedy verification launch the
TileLang kernels; each owner declares the calls it launches where it
registered the Triton kernels' warmups, including probabilistic
drafting's and the full-vocabulary greedy draft's, which compiled at
first launch before. The Triton kernels stay as the tests' reference.

use_fp64_gumbel now fails at startup: the TileLang draw is FP32 only.

